---
import GuidePage from '../../components/GuidePage.astro';
import type { FaqItem } from '../../data/faq';
import { product } from '../../data/product';

const faqs: readonly FaqItem[] = [
	{
		question: 'Is AI Agency Engine a real offer?',
		answer: `Yes. ${product.vendor} is the named vendor, the product site names ADD Marketing Group, LLC, and the pages publish a ${product.advertisedEntryPrice.label} price and a class schedule. That shows a real product launch. It does not prove the training produces clients.`,
	},
	{
		question: 'Did this review test the class?',
		answer:
			'No. This page is based on the public product site and the public launch details. It did not purchase a seat, attend the class, or run Murage.',
	},
	{
		question: 'Do the income examples prove it works?',
		answer:
			'No. The seller uses $500 to $1,000 a month per client, and a $1,000 fee in the Summit Roofing simulation, as illustrations. They are not customer earnings this review verified.',
	},
];

const rows = [
	{
		verified: `${product.vendor} is named as the vendor, and the product site names ADD Marketing Group, LLC.`,
		open: 'Career and sales totals on the partner page were not audited here.',
	},
	{
		verified: `A ${product.advertisedEntryPrice.label} front end is advertised, with a cart window of ${product.schedule.cartOpens} to ${product.schedule.cartCloses}.`,
		open: 'Lessons, support, and refund terms inside that price are not itemized.',
	},
	{
		verified: `A live class is scheduled for ${product.schedule.masterclass}, weekdays at ${product.schedule.masterclassTime}.`,
		open: 'No day-by-day syllabus is published, and this review has not attended.',
	},
	{
		verified: 'Murage screenshots show a team proposal, a research page, held email drafts, and a morning brief that waits for confirmation.',
		open: 'Those demos are not described as the full contents of the paid seat.',
	},
	{
		verified: `Optional offers are priced at $37, $97, $197, and $497. The Complete Package is limited to the ${product.schedule.earlySession}, ${product.schedule.earlySessionTime} session.`,
		open: 'Most of those offers do not describe what the buyer receives.',
	},
	{
		verified: 'Summit Roofing is labeled a simulated test, with an illustrated $1,000 monthly fee.',
		open: 'That fee, and the $10,000 to $20,000 headlines, are not verified results.',
	},
];
---

<GuidePage
	title="Is AI Agency Engine Legit? What the Public Offer Shows"
	description="Is AI Agency Engine legit? A named seller, a $47 class, and Murage demos you can inspect, separated from income claims that remain examples."
	label="Legitimacy"
	h1="Is AI Agency Engine Legit? What We Could Verify Before You Pay"
	crumb="Legitimacy"
	path="/is-ai-agency-engine-legit/"
	related={['/ai-agency-engine-pros-and-cons/', '/ai-agency-engine-pricing/', '/ai-agency-engine-masterclass/']}
	faqs={faqs}
	cta="See the Current Offer Details"
	closingTitle="A real offer is still worth reading at checkout"
	closingText="You can confirm the seller, the $47 price, and the dates. Open the current offer to see the lesson list, the refund rule, and the real total."
>
	<p class="lede" slot="lede">
		AI Agency Engine is a real, dated offer from {product.vendor}, with a {product.advertisedEntryPrice.label} front end and a live class on the calendar. The Murage screenshots show a specific workflow. The income headlines are the seller’s math, not a result this review verified.
	</p>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>What the offer actually is</h2>
			<p class="measure">
				The product is marketed as a way to offer AI-assisted work to local businesses: research a website, show a demo, and prepare the email. The free registration covers three videos, Murage, and an Early Bird seat. The paid piece is the front end and the five-day class. <a href="/ai-agency-engine-pricing/">Review the AI Agency Engine pricing</a> before treating every number on the sales page as one purchase.
			</p>
			<p class="measure">
				The partner page also states large career totals for the vendor. This review did not audit those figures, so they stay outside the verified column.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section band">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>What we could verify, and what you should still check</h2>
			<div class="table-wrap">
				<table class="offer-table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">What the public pages show</th>
							<th scope="col">What is still open</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{
							rows.map((row) => (
								<tr>
									<td data-label="What the public pages show">{row.verified}</td>
									<td data-label="What is still open">{row.open}</td>
								</tr>
							))
						}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>The $1,000 example is a pitch, not proof of earnings</h2>
			<p class="measure">
				The offer page walks Murage through Summit Roofing and labels the charge at $1,000 a month. It calls the walkthrough a simulated test. A sample price in a demo is not a customer result, and multiplying it into $10,000 or $20,000 a month does not make it one.
			</p>
			<p class="measure">
				That leaves a practical conclusion. The offer is specific enough to inspect: a named seller, a published price, and a workflow you can look at. It is not specific enough to treat the income examples as evidence. <a href="/ai-agency-engine-pros-and-cons/">The pros and cons</a> turn that into a fit question. <a href="/ai-agency-engine-masterclass/">The live class dates</a> are schedule claims, not a lesson plan. <a href="/review-methodology/">How this review was prepared</a> lists the sources.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section band">
		<div class="container">
			<h2>Read these on the order page</h2>
			<ul class="note-list">
				<li>The checkout total, including any bump that is already selected.</li>
				<li>The refund terms, which are not stated on the pages reviewed here.</li>
				<li>The lesson list for the {product.advertisedEntryPrice.label} seat.</li>
				<li>Any AI subscription you would pay yourself.</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>
</GuidePage>
